# {{ project_slug }}

A [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io/) analytics app hosted as a Databricks App, combining TPCH analytics (via SQL warehouse) with an editable master-data table backed by [Lakebase](https://docs.databricks.com/en/lakebase/index.html) (managed Postgres).

## Prerequisites

- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) v0.230+, authenticated (`databricks auth login`)
- A workspace with Databricks Apps and Lakebase enabled
- A running SQL warehouse (the bundle auto-resolves one named "Serverless Starter Warehouse", or override `warehouse_id`)

## What's here

```
app/
├── app.py              # Streamlit app (Analytics + Master Data tabs)
├── app.yaml            # Databricks App entrypoint config
└── requirements.txt
resources/
├── apps/app.yml                       # Databricks App resource
├── postgres_projects/lakebase.yml     # Lakebase project (managed Postgres)
├── postgres_branches/production.yml   # Protected production branch
└── postgres_endpoints/primary.yml     # Autoscaling read/write endpoint
```

## Two-step deploy

Lakebase resources must exist before the app can connect to them.

**Step 1 — provision Lakebase:**

```bash
databricks bundle deploy --target dev
```

After it completes, open **Lakebase** in the Databricks UI and copy:

- **PGHOST** — endpoint hostname (Connect modal)
- **ENDPOINT_NAME** — endpoint resource path (Computes tab, e.g. `projects/.../branches/.../endpoints/primary`)

**Step 2 — deploy the app with connection details:**

```bash
databricks bundle deploy --target dev \
  --var="lakebase_pghost=<host>" \
  --var="lakebase_endpoint=<endpoint-path>"
```

The app appears under **Apps** in the Databricks UI.

## Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `warehouse_id` | _(auto-resolved)_ | SQL warehouse used for the Analytics tab |
| `lakebase_project_id` | `{{ cfg.lakebase_project_id }}` | Lakebase project ID |
| `lakebase_min_cu` | `{{ cfg.lakebase_min_cu }}` | Minimum compute units for the Lakebase endpoint |
| `lakebase_max_cu` | `{{ cfg.lakebase_max_cu }}` | Maximum compute units for the Lakebase endpoint |
| `lakebase_pghost` | _(set after first deploy)_ | Endpoint hostname |
| `lakebase_endpoint` | _(set after first deploy)_ | Endpoint resource path |

## Troubleshooting

- **App fails to connect to Postgres on first deploy** — expected before Step 2; `lakebase_pghost`/`lakebase_endpoint` default to placeholders until you provide real values.
- **OAuth token errors** — tokens expire after 1 hour and are refreshed automatically per-connection; if you see stale-credential errors, confirm the app's service principal has access to the Lakebase endpoint.

Add Python packages to `app/requirements.txt` and redeploy — the runtime installs them on app startup.
